index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c077520ac3b88650a9713a30dad0e1e1638bb9f2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bench/aws/TEARDOWN.md
@@ -0,0 +1,137 @@
+# AWS benchmark jobs: launch, collect, tear down (WP11)
+
+Scope: DESIGN.md §12.3–12.4. Each launch needs the user's explicit approval (H-5). The
+lead launches instances himself through the AWS API; this directory only provides the
+bundle, the user data and the collector.
+
+**Constraints by design:** no IAM role or instance profile, no SSH key pair, no
+security-group changes (default group, no inbound rule is needed), no credentials in either
+repository. The instance pulls one bundle from a pre-signed S3 URL, runs one job, prints its
+results to the serial console as framed base64, powers off, and terminates.
+
+## Jobs
+
+| `__JOB__` | What | Suggested `MAXMIN` | Instance |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `b3_paced` | B3 paced sustainable links and latency CDFs (1 MS/s; page targets 0.25/0.5/1 ms; L doubled while sustainable; 5 s warm-up, 60 s, 3 reps) | 130 | c6i.8xlarge (and once on c6i.metal) |
+| `b4_paced` | B4 paced + async control loop, 10 Hz–10 kHz, timed and asap, 3 reps | 130 | c6i.8xlarge |
+| `b5_v1_vs_sremu` | B5 v1-as-committed (+ the one import fix) vs sremu, same host | 60 | c6i.8xlarge |
+| `b2_server_point` | B1 kernels + B2 lockstep slices S1, S6 (thread scaling), S4, S2 (the "large server" point) | 130 | c6i.8xlarge or c6i.metal |
+| `eb3_paced_controller` | E-B3 timing demonstration (external TDMA controller, paced + async) | 130 | c6i.8xlarge |
+| `smoke` | quick B2 (S1, S6) + quick B3 + a 7 s B4 paced run: checks the whole path cheaply | 45 | any (e.g. c6i.2xlarge) |
+| `selftest` | no sremu run; checks download, verify, pack and the console channel | 20 | any |
+
+Every job sizes itself to finish within 85 min (`--budget-min`, reduced automatically when
+`MAXMIN` is smaller); `user_data.sh` reserves 25 min for packing and streaming. If a job
+still overruns, `timeout` sends SIGINT at the end of its slot: the running suite writes its
+partial run directory (`"interrupted"` in `summary.json` and `meta.json`) within 45 s, and
+`status.json` records `"interrupted": true`. Each paced suite's `summary.json` states
+whether the run met the §12.3 protocol (`protocol_12_3.meets_12_3`).
+
+## 1. Before launch (laptop)
+
+- [ ] Commit the sremu tree (the bundle records `sremu_commit` and `sremu_dirty`).
+- [ ] `python -m bench.b5_v1 --nodes 2 --reps 1` once, so the v1 scratch copy
+      `research/scratch/v1_bench` exists with the import fix (never touches `D:\ris-sim`).
+- [ ] `python bench/aws/make_bundle.py build` → `runs/aws_bundle/sremu_bundle_<commit8>.tar.gz`,
+      `.sha256`, `.bundle_info.json`. Check `sremu_dirty` is `false` and
+      `untracked_not_included` is empty (otherwise commit first, or pass
+      `--include-untracked`, which is recorded in the manifest).
+- [ ] Optional rehearsal without AWS: `python bench/aws/dryrun_local.py --job selftest`
+      (about 1 min in WSL2) or `--job smoke` (installs the pinned wheels from PyPI inside
+      WSL2; about 30 min on the laptop's connection).
+- [ ] Laptop pilot of the same job done (H-5): e.g. `python -m bench.b3_paced --quick`.
+- [ ] Price check in the console for the instance type and region (cost [UNVERIFIED]).
+
+## 2. Launch (one instance per job)
+
+- [ ] Upload the bundle to a private S3 bucket, tags `project=sremu`, `owner=<you>`.
+- [ ] Pre-sign a GET URL valid for 15 min (900 s). The instance downloads in its first
+      minute, so launch right after pre-signing.
+- [ ] Render the user data:
+      `python bench/aws/make_bundle.py render --job b3_paced --url "<presigned>" --sha256 <sha> --maxmin 130 -o ud_b3.sh`
+      (refuses non-https URLs, unknown jobs and > 16 KB).
+- [ ] RunInstances with: Ubuntu 24.04 LTS amd64 AMI (Canonical SSM parameter
+      `/aws/service/canonical/ubuntu/server/24.04/stable/current/amd64/hvm/ebs-gp3/ami-id`),
+      the instance type above, `InstanceInitiatedShutdownBehavior=terminate`, **no**
+      `IamInstanceProfile`, **no** `KeyName`, the default security group, a subnet with
+      outbound internet access (S3 and PyPI), root gp3 30 GiB with
+      `DeleteOnTermination=true`, tags `project=sremu`, `owner=<you>`, `job=<job>`,
+      `UserData` = the rendered file.
+- [ ] Record: instance id, type, AZ, AMI id, launch time, bundle SHA-256, job, MAXMIN.
+
+The first thing the instance does is `shutdown -h +MAXMIN` (hard cap; with the shutdown
+behaviour `terminate` this also terminates it).
+
+## 3. Collect while it runs
+
+- [ ] Poll `GetConsoleOutput(InstanceId, Latest=true)` every 5 s or faster (Nitro instances
+      return only the most recent 64 KB, about 8 s of streamed output at 8000 characters/s)
+      and save every reply as its own file, e.g. `runs/aws_console/<job>/snap_00001.json`.
+      The raw API reply (base64 `Output`), boto3's reply (decoded `Output`) and plain
+      console text are all accepted. `SREMU-LOG|<job>|<t>|...` lines show progress (a
+      heartbeat every 60 s). A minimal poller, run on the laptop with the lead's own
+      credentials (none are stored in either repository):
+
+      ```python
+      import json, pathlib, time
+      import boto3
+
+      ec2 = boto3.client("ec2", region_name="<region>")
+      out = pathlib.Path("runs/aws_console/<job>")
+      out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+      for k in range(1, 100_000):
+          r = ec2.get_console_output(InstanceId="<i-...>", Latest=True)
+          text = r.get("Output", "")
+          (out / f"snap_{k:05d}.json").write_text(json.dumps({"Output": text}), encoding="utf-8")
+          if "SREMU-DONE" in text:
+              break
+          time.sleep(4)
+      ```
+
+      Where snapshots cannot be written to files (e.g. a sandbox that only returns values),
+      keep only the lines starting with `SREMU` (deduplicated) and save those;
+      `collect_console.py` needs nothing else.
+- [ ] When `SREMU-META` / `SREMU|...` lines appear, the results are being streamed: three
+      complete passes with 20 s pauses, throttled to 8000 characters/s, then `SREMU-END` and
+      `SREMU-DONE`. A 300 KB result takes about 1 min per pass.
+- [ ] `python bench/aws/collect_console.py runs/aws_console/<job>/snap_*.json --job <job> --out runs/aws_results`
+      exit 0 = complete and verified (per-chunk CRC-32 and whole-archive SHA-256) and
+      unpacked to `runs/aws_results/<job>/`; exit 2 = chunks missing (listed): keep
+      polling until the last pass ends; exit 1 = inconsistent data (do not use).
+- [ ] If the console never shows `SREMU-META`, read the `SREMU-LOG` lines: the failure
+      reason (download, checksum, apt, pip, job exit code) is printed and the job log is
+      still streamed whenever the bundle step got far enough.
+
+## 4. Tear down (every time)
+
+- [ ] DescribeInstances: state `terminated` (expected within a minute of `SREMU-DONE`; at
+      the latest at `MAXMIN`). If not, TerminateInstances now.
+- [ ] DescribeVolumes filtered by the instance id / tag `project=sremu`: none left
+      (root volume has `DeleteOnTermination=true`).
+- [ ] No Elastic IP, ENI, snapshot or AMI was created (DescribeAddresses,
+      DescribeNetworkInterfaces, DescribeSnapshots/Images with `Owner=self`, tag filter).
+- [ ] Delete the bundle object (and the bucket, when the campaign ends).
+- [ ] Note the instance-hours and the console's cost estimate.
+- [ ] Add the instance record (id, type, AZ, AMI, times, bundle SHA-256, job, MAXMIN,
+      collect_console status) to `runs/aws_results/aws_runs.json`; the run manifests
+      carry `aws_instance` {type, id} read from DMI on the instance.
+
+## Notes
+
+- Paced numbers for the paper come only from these Linux runs (DESIGN.md §12.3); laptop
+  paced numbers stay labelled "Windows, not representative".
+- The CPU governor is set to `performance` only where the VM exposes cpufreq (usually not
+  on c6i virtual instances; the result records `governor=unavailable` then).
+- CPU split: the cores of CPU 0 and CPU 1, with their SMT siblings (on c6i usually
+  CPUs 0, 1, 16, 17), take the OS and the benchmark's client processes (ZMQ data clients,
+  controller processes; `SREMU_CLIENT_CPUS`, applied by `bench.pin_client_cpus`); the job is
+  pinned with `taskset` to every other CPU and uses `NUMBA_NUM_THREADS` = their number
+  (28 on c6i.8xlarge). Reason, measured on the laptop: numba's OpenMP kernels slow down by
+  orders of magnitude when another busy process shares their CPUs (a spinning client or
+  background jobs), because every parallel region waits for its slowest thread.
+- Serial-console output on `c6i.metal` [UNVERIFIED]: check `GetConsoleOutput` with a
+  `selftest` job before a long metal run.
+- The bundle's dependency pins come from the laptop venv; if a pin cannot be installed, the
+  job continues unpinned and leaves `PINS_NOT_HONORED` in the results (the instance's
+  `pip freeze` is in `sysinfo.json` either way).
